     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Wed, Jan 4, 2017 at 5:53 PM, Paul Hoekstra <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">paul.h...@naturalis.nl</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I would like to put clade labels on my tree, however one of the clades consist of just 1 specimen.<div><br></div><div>For example, when using the following tree:</div><div><div>set.seed(1)</div><div>tr &lt;- rtree(4)</div><div><br></div><div><div>Then to assign tips 2 to 4 to clade A and tip 1 to clade B I tried this:</div></div><div><br></div><div>p &lt;- ggtree(tr) + geom_cladelabel(node=6, label = &quot;A&quot;, barsize = 2)<br></div><div>p + geom_cladelabel(node=1, label = &quot;B&quot;)</div></div><div><br></div><div>But then I get the warning that the input node is a tip and clade B isn&#39;t displayed. I would like to see a black square for clade B, so I also tried geom_point2, but in that function &#39;offset&#39; and &#39;hjust&#39; don&#39;t work. </div><div><br></div><div>How could I resolve this?</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks in advance,</div><div>Paul</div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
